{"meta":{"ticker":"VTV","as_of_date":"2026-07-31","performance_as_of":"2026-07-31","generated_at":"2026-08-01 07:51:55"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"VTV","fund_name":"Vanguard Value ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Value","issuer":"Vanguard","index_name":"CRSP US Large Value","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0003,"aum":188242842396,"holdings_count":326,"inception_date":"2004-01-26","overall_score":9.86123955947136,"overall_rank":2,"sector_diversification_score":6.81417079207921},"description":{"tsi_description":"VTV is a low-cost large-cap value ETF that tracks the CRSP Large Cap Value Index and provides broad exposure to established U.S. companies trading at relatively attractive valuations. The fund emphasizes traditional value characteristics such as low price-to-earnings ratios, low price-to-book ratios, and higher dividend yields while maintaining diversified exposure across the U.S. equity market. Unlike more aggressive value strategies, VTV prioritizes stability and broad diversification, which has historically helped it avoid severe drawdowns during difficult market environments. The ETF is heavily tilted toward Financials, Health Care, and Consumer Staples and generally appeals to investors seeking steady long-term value exposure with below-market volatility. Overall, VTV offers a conservative and highly efficient approach to passive large-cap value investing.","strategy_steps":["Selects securities from the CRSP U.S. Total Market Index representing approximately the top 85% of total U.S. market capitalization.","Uses a float-adjusted market capitalization weighting methodology.","Applies a rules-based multi-factor framework to separate value stocks from growth stocks.","Evaluates value characteristics using book-to-price, future earnings-to-price, historical earnings-to-price, dividend-to-price, and sales-to-price ratios.","Evaluates growth characteristics using 